{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790986853,"nonce":"5bAUnEYrVTBlnACTrXKNaPLReTM=","title":"Easing::evaluate ignores a cubic bezier's x control points","message":"crates/blinc_theme/src/tokens/animation.rs Easing::evaluate approximates CubicBezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) by evaluating only the y polynomial at parameter t (cubic_bezier_approximate), ignoring x1 and x2. CSS's cubic-bezier is y at the parameter where x(s) = t. For the theme's STANDARD curve (0.25, 0.10, 0.25, 1.0, i.e. CSS 'ease') at t = 0.5 the approximation gives 0.5375; CSS gives 0.8024. Every theme curve is affected (HYBRID_NAV, the spring curves, EMPHASIZED...), so motion driven through evaluate runs on a different curve than the CSS the theme also exports. ashui now solves for s (Newton steps, bisection fallback) in EasingTools.evaluate (haxe/ashui/theme/Easing.hx), checked against CSS's value. Found by ashui while building transitions on the theme's curves.","files":null}]}